# Wobble Rush 3D — CF Workers WebSocket Multiplayer: Research Report
### Hono + Durable Object + WebSocket Hibernation + wrangler 4.x + static assets

Verified against this repo's installed versions: **wrangler 4.114.0**, **hono 4.12.32**, **@cloudflare/workers-types 5.20260724.1**. All doc pages below were fetched live (dated 2026) during this research.

---

## 1. Exact `wrangler.jsonc` for wrangler 4.x

Two equivalent forms exist for declaring the DO class. **They are mutually exclusive** — pick one.

**Form A — modern declarative `exports` (recommended for new projects in 2026):**
```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "wobble-rush-3d",
  "main": "src/index.ts",                 // Hono entry (app.fetch)
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-24",
  // "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat_v2"],  // only if you need Node builtins

  "assets": {                              // static assets binding + serving
    "directory": "./public",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application", // SPA fallback to index.html
    "run_worker_first": ["/room/*", "/api/*"]         // route game/API to Hono, not asset handler
  },

  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [
      { "name": "ROOMS", "class_name": "RoomDurableObject" }
    ]
  },

  // Declarative class lifecycle (replaces legacy `migrations`). SQLite = required for new namespaces.
  "exports": {
    "RoomDurableObject": { "type": "durable-object", "storage": "sqlite" }
  },

  "routes": [
    { "pattern": "wobble-rush.mengmota.com", "custom_domain": true }
  ],

  "limits": { "cpu_ms": 300000 }           // optional: raise DO/Worker CPU to 5 min (default 30s)
}
```

**Form B — legacy `migrations` with `new_sqlite_classes` (still supported; what the official hibernation example uses):**
```jsonc
{
  "name": "wobble-rush-3d",
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-24",
  "assets": { "directory": "./public", "binding": "ASSETS", "not_found_handling": "single-page-application", "run_worker_first": ["/room/*", "/api/*"] },
  "durable_objects": { "bindings": [ { "name": "ROOMS", "class_name": "RoomDurableObject" } ] },
  "migrations": [ { "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["RoomDurableObject"] } ],
  "routes": [ { "pattern": "wobble-rush.mengmota.com", "custom_domain": true } ]
}
```

TOML equivalent of the DO/migrations block:
```toml
[[durable_objects.bindings]]
name = "ROOMS"
class_name = "RoomDurableObject"

[[migrations]]
tag = "v1"
new_sqlite_classes = ["RoomDurableObject"]
```

Key config notes (all verified in wrangler 4.x config doc, last updated 2026-07-24):
- `name`, `main`, `compatibility_date` are the only required top-level keys (`main` optional only for assets-only workers).
- `[assets]` keys: `directory`, `binding` (exposes `env.ASSETS.fetch(request)`), `not_found_handling` (`"single-page-application"` | `"404-page"`), `run_worker_first` (`true` or route-pattern array). By default, asset-matching requests **skip** the Worker; `run_worker_first` forces Hono to run first. Use `["/room/*","/api/*"]` so Hono handles WS upgrades + REST while static files bypass the Worker.
- `new_sqlite_classes` is correct for new SQLite-backed DOs. `new_classes` (without `_sqlite`) creates **legacy KV-backed** namespaces — **no longer allowed for new accounts**; SQLite is the only path for new namespaces. Free plan only supports SQLite.
- `routes[].custom_domain: true` is how you request a **Custom Domain** (not a route) in wrangler config. The pattern is the bare hostname. Cloudflare auto-creates the DNS record + Advanced Certificate on deploy.

Docs:
- Wrangler configuration: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/configuration/
- Static Assets: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/
- DO class exports (modern): https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/reference/durable-objects/
- Legacy `migrations`/`new_sqlite_classes`: https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/reference/durable-objects-migrations/

