## 2. WebSocket Hibernation pattern (minimal correct sketch)

The Hibernation API lets the DO be evicted from memory while WS connections stay open; **Billable Duration (GB-s) does not accrue while hibernated**. Core surface (all on `this.ctx`, current `cloudflare:workers` types):

- `this.ctx.acceptWebSocket(server)` — accept + mark hibernatable (NOT `ws.accept()`).
- `this.ctx.getWebSockets(tag?)` — all sockets (optionally filtered by tag).
- `this.ctx.getWebSocketById(id)` — lookup by id.
- `this.ctx.setWebSocketAutoResponse(new WebSocketRequestResponsePair('ping','pong'))` — app-level ping/pong that **does not wake** the hibernated DO.
- `ws.serializeAttachment(value)` / `ws.deserializeAttachment()` — per-socket state that **survives hibernation** (must be JSON-serializable).
- Handlers on the DO class: `webSocketMessage(ws, message: string|ArrayBuffer)`, `webSocketClose(ws, code, reason, wasClean)`, `webSocketError(ws, error)`.

```ts
import { DurableObject } from "cloudflare:workers";

interface ConnState { id: string; name: string; }

export class RoomDurableObject extends DurableObject<Env> {
  sessions = new Map<WebSocket, ConnState>();   // rebuilt on every wake

  constructor(ctx: DurableObjectState, env: Env) {
    super(ctx, env);
    // On wake, the constructor runs FIRST. Restore the in-memory map from hibernated sockets.
    for (const ws of this.ctx.getWebSockets()) {
      const s = ws.deserializeAttachment() as ConnState | null;
      if (s) this.sessions.set(ws, s);
    }
    // App-level heartbeat that does not interrupt hibernation:
    this.ctx.setWebSocketAutoResponse(new WebSocketRequestResponsePair("ping", "pong"));
  }

  // Worker forwards the upgrade request here via stub.fetch(c.req.raw)
  async fetch(request: Request): Promise<Response> {
    if (request.headers.get("Upgrade") !== "websocket") {
      return new Response("Expected Upgrade: websocket", { status: 426 });
    }
    const [client, server] = Object.values(new WebSocketPair());
    const id = crypto.randomUUID();
    const state: ConnState = { id, name: "" };
    this.ctx.acceptWebSocket(server);   // hibernatable accept
    server.serializeAttachment(state);   // persists across hibernation
    this.sessions.set(server, state);
    return new Response(null, { status: 101, webSocket: client });
  }

  async webSocketMessage(ws: WebSocket, msg: ArrayBuffer | string) {
    const state = this.sessions.get(ws) ?? ws.deserializeAttachment() as ConnState;
    const data = typeof msg === "string" ? JSON.parse(msg) : parseBinary(msg);
    if (data.t === "join") { state.name = data.name; ws.serializeAttachment(state); }
    // relay positions to everyone else (broadcast)
    for (const peer of this.ctx.getWebSockets()) {
      if (peer !== ws) peer.send(JSON.stringify({ t: "state", from: state.id, ...data }));
    }
  }

  async webSocketClose(ws: WebSocket, code: number, reason: string, wasClean: boolean) {
    // compat_date >= 2026-04-07 auto-replies to Close frames; close() is safe but optional.
    ws.close(code, reason);
    this.sessions.delete(ws);
    // optionally broadcast "leave"
  }

  async webSocketError(ws: WebSocket, err: unknown) {
    console.error("ws error", err);
    this.sessions.delete(ws);
  }
}
```

Notes from the docs:
- When a hibernated DO receives a message, the runtime **re-runs the `constructor`** then delivers the message — so keep the constructor cheap and rebuild ephemeral state from `getWebSockets()` + `deserializeAttachment()`.
- `webSocketMessage` is **not** called for control frames (ping/pong/close).
- Hibernation only applies when the DO is the **server**. Outgoing WebSockets don't hibernate (and an active outgoing WS keeps the DO alive up to 15 min).
- `alarms`, incoming requests, `scheduled`, `setTimeout`/`setInterval` **prevent hibernation** while pending.

Docs:
- Use WebSockets / Hibernation API: https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/best-practices/websockets/
- Full example: https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/examples/websocket-hibernation-server/
- Workers runtime WebSocket API: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/websockets/

