## 4. Local dev with `wrangler dev`

`wrangler dev` runs Miniflare locally and fully supports DOs + WebSockets end-to-end. **Gotcha:** hibernation is *not* truly simulated locally — the DO is never evicted from memory — but all hibernation handlers (`webSocketMessage`, etc.) **are** still delivered, so your handler logic tests correctly. (Behavior has been this way since wrangler ≥ 3.13.2 / Miniflare v3.20231016.0.)

Testing two browser clients locally:
1. `bun run dev` (your script = `bun run build && wrangler dev`). Default local URL `http://localhost:8787`.
2. Open **two** browser contexts (two tabs, or two Playwright `browser.newContext()`s — your goal doc's C4 asks for exactly this). Both navigate to the same room code, e.g. both open the lobby, join code `ABCD`, and connect to `ws://localhost:8787/room/ABCD/ws`.
3. Both clients resolve to the **same local DO instance** for code `ABCD` (Miniflare keeps one DO per name in `.wrangler/state/v3/durable-objects`), so they see each other's position relays.

Gotchas:
- **Mixed content:** on plain `http://localhost:8787` use `ws://` (not `wss://`). If you expose dev over HTTPS via a tunnel, you need `wss://`. Browsers block `ws://` from an `https://` page.
- **State persistence:** Miniflare persists DO SQLite in `.wrangler/state/`. Stale room state across runs? `rm -rf .wrangler/state` to reset.
- **`--remote` vs `--local`:** wrangler 4 defaults to local mode. `--remote` runs against real CF infra (uses your account quota, real hibernation) — only use if you specifically need real eviction behavior.
- The two clients must share the exact room-code normalization (uppercase/trim) or they land in different DO instances.
- `wrangler dev` does **not** auto-create the custom domain; test via `localhost`. Custom-domain DNS/cert only happens on `wrangler deploy`.

Docs:
- Local development (Miniflare, DO, websockets): https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/local-development/
- Wrangler dev / Static Assets debugging: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/dev/

