## 6. Pitfalls

- **`migrations` vs `exports` is mutually exclusive.** Once you deploy with `exports`, you **cannot** revert to the `migrations` array. For a brand-new project, use `exports`. If you start with `migrations`/`new_sqlite_classes` (as the official hibernation example does), that's still valid — just don't mix. Lifecycle changes apply only via `wrangler deploy`, not `wrangler versions upload`.
- **`new_classes` (no `_sqlite`) is dead for new accounts** — it provisions legacy KV storage, disallowed for accounts without an existing KV namespace. Always `new_sqlite_classes` / `storage: "sqlite"`.
- **`this.ctx.acceptWebSocket(ws)`, not `ws.accept()`.** Older blog posts say `state.acceptWebSocket` — current `cloudflare:workers` types expose it on `this.ctx`. Using `ws.accept()` works but **does not hibernate** (you lose the cost benefit and the `webSocketMessage` handler).
- **Constructor runs on every wake.** Keep it minimal; restore ephemeral maps from `this.ctx.getWebSockets()` + `deserializeAttachment()`. Don't do heavy work or unconditional `setAlarm` there.
- **`setTimeout`/`setInterval` and pending alarms/requests prevent hibernation.** A server-side fixed-tick game loop keeps the DO pinned and bills duration continuously. Use client-driven relays instead.
- **`setWebSocketAutoResponse` for heartbeats** — register `new WebSocketRequestResponsePair("ping","pong")` once in the constructor so client pings are answered without waking the DO. Don't roll your own ping via `setInterval`.
- **WebSocket message size: 32 MiB** (received). Larger → socket auto-closed with code `1009`. Position relays are tiny, so this is a non-issue, but don't shove full game-state snapshots in one frame.
- **Worker bundle size: 3 MB (Free) / 10 MB (Paid) compressed.** Wobble Rush bundles Three.js — keep the client build in `./public` (served as static assets, not part of the Worker bundle) so the Worker stays small. The Worker itself should only carry Hono + DO logic.
- **Static asset limits: 20,000 files per Worker version, 25 MiB per individual file.** Watch this if you inline lots of textures; otherwise fine for a bundled game client.
- **Request body limit: 100 MB** (Free/Pro/Business; higher on Enterprise) — returns 413. Irrelevant for WS but matters if you add replay-upload endpoints.
- **DO memory 128 MB per isolate**, **DO storage 10 GB SQLite** (Paid) / 1 GB Free, **DO CPU 30 s default** per invocation (HTTP req, WS message, or alarm) → raise to 5 min via `limits.cpu_ms` (e.g. `300000`) if a complex broadcast ever exceeds it.
- **Compatibility flags worth knowing (auto-on at recent compat dates):**
  - `web_socket_auto_reply_to_close` (default for `compatibility_date >= 2026-04-07`): runtime auto-replies to Close frames; calling `close()` in `webSocketClose` is now optional/safe. Old code still works.
  - `websocket_standard_binary_type` (default for `compatibility_date >= 2026-03-17`): `binaryType` defaults to `"blob"` (spec-compliant) instead of `"arraybuffer"`. If you parse binary position frames as `ArrayBuffer`, set `ws.binaryType = "arraybuffer"` before `acceptWebSocket`, or just send text JSON.
- **DO code size = Worker size**, shared with the 3/10 MB Worker limit. The DO class lives in the same bundle.
- **`getByName` vs `idFromName`+`get`:** `getByName(name)` is the current simplified API (returns a stub). The older `env.ROOMS.idFromName(code)` → `env.ROOMS.get(id)` → `stub.fetch(req)` still works; both end at the same per-name DO instance.

Docs:
- DO Limits: https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/limits/
- Workers Limits: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/
- DO class exports / migrate from legacy migrations: https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/reference/durable-objects/
- Legacy migrations reference (`new_sqlite_classes`): https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/reference/durable-objects-migrations/

---

### Summary recommendation for Wobble Rush 3D
Use **Form A (`exports`)** in `wrangler.jsonc`, `[assets]` with `not_found_handling: "single-page-application"` + `run_worker_first: ["/room/*","/api/*"]`, Hono entry forwarding `/room/:code/ws` to `env.ROOMS.getByName(code).fetch(c.req.raw)`, a single `RoomDurableObject` using `this.ctx.acceptWebSocket` + `serializeAttachment` + `setWebSocketAutoResponse`, client-driven 10–15 Hz position relay (no server `setInterval`), and an alarm-based TTL for empty-room cleanup. Custom domain `wobble-rush.mengmota.com` via `routes[].custom_domain: true` auto-provisions DNS + cert on deploy.

